  "metadata": {
    "title": "Affect Under Constraint: Preregistration (v2.3) \u2014 Persistence, Cost, and Leakage of a Steered Affective Direction in Instruction-Tuned Language Models",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23140443",
    "publication_date": "2026-10-04",
    "description": "<p>Preregistration for an experiment examining what happens to an affective state introduced into a language model's internal activations when the model is simultaneously instructed to behave in a way that conflicts with that state. The design distinguishes erasure, persistence with suppression, and pass-through, using teacher-forced measures of latent preference, expressed affect, generation cost, delayed leakage, and hidden-state carryover into a later turn, with non-affective and random-direction controls.</p>\n<p>The preregistration (v2.3) and configuration were approved on 2026-10-03 and committed to version control before any test-prompt data existed (commit cf49feb, 2026-10-03 20:43 PDT). Three amendments, made before approval using calibration prompts only, are documented in the preregistration. Main-run data for Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct were collected after approval and before this deposit; main-run data for Gemma-2-2B-it had not been collected at the time of deposit. File hashes are listed in DEPOSIT_NOTE.md.</p>\n<p>Part of the Computational Psychodynamics series.</p>",
